# Binary assets must never have their line endings rewritten.
#
# Git decides text-vs-binary by a content heuristic, and it misjudges image
# data that happens to contain no NUL byte. That is not hypothetical here:
# test/fixtures/golden/max5.pgm was the one fixture in the tree git called
# text, so a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true turned the three LFs in
# its "P5\n32 24\n255\n" header into CRLFs. imBinFileReadInteger then consumed
# the \r as the single whitespace byte the PNM spec says follows the maxval,
# the \n became pixel zero, and the whole golden image was read one byte
# late -- 462 of its 768 samples wrong, on Windows only, with the committed
# file and the library both perfectly correct.
#
# Which files the heuristic misjudges depends on their pixel values, so
# regenerating a fixture can silently move the problem to a different file.
# Name the formats instead of trusting the guess.

*.pgm   binary
*.ppm   binary
*.pbm   binary
*.pnm   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.heic  binary
*.avif  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.class binary
